# TierOne AutoBlog — env pattern (owner FULLY-FREE directive, 2026-10-17)
#
# LLM stages (brief/outline/draft) speak OpenAI-compatible protocol to a FREE
# endpoint. Never configure a paid API — free tiers only. Copy to `.env`
# (gitignored) and fill from one of the options below.
#
#   Groq            https://api.groq.com/openai/v1        free API key (console.groq.com/keys)
#   OpenRouter      https://openrouter.ai/api/v1          use `:free`-suffixed model ids
#   local Ollama    http://localhost:11434/v1             no key needed (leave LLM_API_KEY unset)

# Primary free endpoint (required): base URL + model id; key optional (Ollama is keyless).
LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
LLM_API_KEY=gsk_replace_with_your_free_groq_key
LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# Optional cheaper/faster model for narrow tasks (summarize / title-desc).
# Unset = LLM_MODEL is used for everything.
# LLM_MODEL_CHEAP=llama-3.1-8b-instant

# Optional fallback provider, attempted once when the primary transport fails.
# Also free-tier only. Unset = no fallback.
# LLM_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# LLM_FALLBACK_API_KEY=sk-or-your-free_openrouter_key
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# Optional image machinery (Plan 03-05): the ONLY built-in image providers are
# FREE ones — 'procedural' (default: deterministic concept-derived SVG art,
# rendered by sharp to AVIF/WebP/OG-JPEG, zero external calls + zero keys) and
# 'fixture' (the deterministic test lane). Third-party PAID image APIs are
# FORBIDDEN (owner fully-free directive 2026-10-17); forcing PIPELINE_IMAGE_PROVIDER
# to a paid name fails honestly instead of ever constructing the client.
# PIPELINE_IMAGE_FIXTURE=1 selects the fixture provider (no other env needed).
# PIPELINE_IMAGE_PROVIDER=procedural|fixture   (default: procedural)

Keyless note: keyword sources (autocomplete/trends/SERP) are KEYLESS free
signals and need no env at all — governance lives in
content/keywords/spend-ledger.json (request-cap governor).
